# Task 7 – Override and Specialise Behaviour

## Objective
To implement method overriding in Java.

## Method Overriding
The Car class overrides the calculateFee() method of Vehicle
to provide a different parking fee.

## @Override Annotation
The @Override annotation indicates that a method overrides
a method declared in the parent class.

## final Keyword
The final keyword can prevent a variable from being reassigned,
a method from being overridden, or a class from being inherited.

## Object Class Methods
- toString(): Returns vehicle information.
- equals(): Compares vehicle registration numbers.
- hashCode(): Returns a hash code based on the registration number.

## Alternative Concept
A switch statement could calculate fees based on vehicle type.
However, adding a new type may require modifying the existing
calculateFee() method.

## Complexity Analysis
- Fee calculation: O(1)
